@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpi-il35-nouns`
IMPORT `cpi-il35-published-figures`
IMPORT `cpi-il35-index-rules`
IMPORT `ito-s120b-index`
IMPORT `nii-s334-index`

-- Tests for row IL-35. Every expected value was worked by hand from the Bureau's JSON (the two files in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/data/) BEFORE it was asserted, the arithmetic shown beside it. A failing assertion is a
-- finding; no expected value was edited to match the code. The readings the JSON prints are quoted as (year-month: value, base).
-- Abbreviations used below:  L = "linking through the Bureau's coefficients" (fork F1, reading 1),
--                            P = "the percentage the Bureau published for twelve months" (fork F1, reading 2).
-- Hand arithmetic is in exact fractions; decimals are the Bureau's one-decimal figures, so "a / b" is the exact quotient.

§ `Helpers for the tests`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the reading for` y `month` m MEANS
    r's `the value of the reading`
    WHERE r MEANS `the reading the Bureau published for` (`the calendar month in year` y `, number` m)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base year of the reading for` y `month` m MEANS
    r's `the base year of the reading`
    WHERE r MEANS `the reading the Bureau published for` (`the calendar month in year` y `, number` m)

-- the month a reading is of, for "published last before" tests: returns its running number as year*12+month-1.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year-and-month of the reading last published before the start of` y `month` m MEANS
    (r's `the year the reading is of`) TIMES 100 PLUS (r's `the month the reading is of`)
    WHERE r MEANS `the reading last published before the start of` (`the calendar month in year` y `, number` m)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year-and-month of the reading last published before the end of` y `month` m MEANS
    (r's `the year the reading is of`) TIMES 100 PLUS (r's `the month the reading is of`)
    WHERE r MEANS `the reading last published before the end of` (`the calendar month in year` y `, number` m)

DECIDE link IS `readings of two bases are compared by linking them through the Bureau's coefficients`
DECIDE pct  IS `a rise over twelve months is the percent the Bureau published for the twelve months`
DECIDE decl IS `a rise across a change of base is declined`

